.TH SDL_GetCurrentDirectory 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetCurrentDirectory \- Get what the system believes is the \(dqcurrent working directory.\(dq
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_filesystem.h>
.PP
.BI "char * SDL_GetCurrentDirectory(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
For systems without a concept of a current working directory, this will still attempt to provide something reasonable\[char46]
.PP
SDL does not provide a means to _change_ the current working directory; for platforms without this concept, this would cause surprises with file access outside of SDL\[char46]
.PP
The returned path is guaranteed to end with a path separator (\(aq\(rs\(rs\(aq on Windows, \(aq/\(aq on most other platforms)\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a UTF-8 string of the current working directory in platform-dependent notation\[char46] NULL if there\(aqs a problem\[char46] This should be freed with
.BR SDL_free ()
when it is no longer needed\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

